&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with software engineers, product managers, and subject matter experts to extract accurate technical detail and drive timely review cycles, including setting deadlines and driving stakeholder alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead documentation work tied to major platform and product initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and develop content for AI consumability and discoverability, including how documentation performs in LLM-mediated search and developer evaluation contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply a structured content approach to ensure documentation serves the right audience at the right stage of their journey, from evaluation through advanced use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to documentation standards, style guidelines, and peer review processes across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior voice in cross-functional planning, advocating for documentation requirements in the product development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner on piloting AI-assisted drafting tools: evaluate output quality, help define what a human must verify before publication, and help build workflows where AI assistance meaningfully improves content and reduces toil.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute content expertise to docs replatforming initiatives by representing structured-content and authoring requirements in tooling evaluations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some of the things we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of technical writing experience, with a strong portfolio of developer-facing or data infrastructure documentation. Writing samples required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work autonomously in ambiguous, fast-paced environments and make sound content decisions without close supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning documentation for complex SaaS, cloud, or data platform products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage SME relationships decisively, including driving review cycles and escalating blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with docs-as-code workflows: Git/GitHub, Markdown, and static site generators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with or strong interest in content architecture, structured authoring, and emerging documentation platform tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication in US English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in a technical field or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong plus: familiarity with how documentation is consumed by AI systems (llms.txt, RAG-friendly chunking, MCP, AI-search visibility), or hands-on experience using LLMs in a content workflow (drafting, evaluating output quality).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have:&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;basic scripting/automation exposure (Python, JavaScript, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
